      "math_academy_id": "q-112657",
      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{b}_{3}$, ${c}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{4}{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{3}=2{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4{b}_{1}-2{b}_{2}+{b}_{3} \\\\  & ={b}_{3}-2{b}_{2}+4{b}_{1} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{3}{b}_{3})+2\\cdot 4(-\\frac{1}{4}{b}_{2})+2(2{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =3{c}_{1}+8{c}_{2}+2{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
